cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "campypump: classify RE-cmeABC efflux pump alleles in Campylobacter genomes"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  campypump classifies the cmeB gene of the Campylobacter cmeABC efflux operon as RE-cmeB, the
  resistance-enhancing variant that raises fluoroquinolone and macrolide MICs, or as wildtype,
  directly from genome assemblies. It replaces a manual BLAST-and-align workflow and reproduces its
  identity values exactly. Alongside the cmeB call it reports identity to a panel of reference
  alleles, the operon context (cmeR, the CmeR operator, cmeA and cmeC), structural classification of
  the CmeR operator, quality-control flags, optional species assignment by whole-genome ANI, and
  figures and allele phylogenies.
